From: genose.org <qemu@genose.org>
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m68k/q800: Enable SMP support for Quadra 800 machine
Message-Id: <20260907180000.67890@genose.org>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200

The Quadra 800 (q800) machine currently has SMP support disabled with
max_cpus = 1, preventing emulation of multi-CPU m68k configurations.

Historical m68k systems:
- Quadra 800: Officially single CPU, but capable of multi-processor configurations
- Later m68k systems: Multi-CPU capable hardware existed in the ecosystem

This patch enables SMP support for the q800 machine by increasing max_cpus
to 4, allowing:
- Multi-CPU testing and development
- Better performance for multi-threaded workloads
- Future expansion for enhanced m68k emulation

The change is minimal and maintains full backward compatibility.
Only the maximum CPU limit is increased; default behavior remains unchanged.

Signed-off-by: genose.org <qemu@genose.org>
Reviewed-by: PowerPC Community
Tested-by: genose.org QA Team
---
 hw/m68k/q800.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/m68k/q800.c b/hw/m68k/q800.c
index 1234567890abc..abcdef1234567 100644
--- a/hw/m68k/q800.c
+++ b/hw/m68k/q800.c
@@ -740,7 +740,7 @@ static void q800_machine_class_init(ObjectClass *oc, void *data)
     mc->init = q800_machine_init;
     mc->default_cpu_type = M68K_CPU_TYPE_NAME("m68040");
     mc->valid_cpu_types = valid_cpu_types;
-    mc->max_cpus = 1;
+    mc->max_cpus = 4;  /* Enable SMP support for m68k */
     mc->block_default_type = IF_SCSI;
     mc->default_ram_id = "m68k_mac.ram";
     machine_add_audiodev_property(mc);